# Leohang Illustrations Skill

When generating article illustrations for Chinese content:

## Visual Rules
- 16:9 horizontal, pure white background, black hand-drawn line art, sparse red/orange/blue Chinese annotations
- Subject 40-60% of canvas, at least 35% whitespace
- One image = one core metaphor or structure
- No PPT, no cute cartoon, no gradients/shadows, no title in top-left corner

## Character: Leohang
Young man, short black hair, rectangular black-framed glasses (always visible, core identifier), black high-collar zip-up jacket, black trousers, white sneakers. Focused, calm, hands-on engineer. Must perform the core action — not decorative.

## Workflow
1. Read article → identify cognitive anchors (key judgments, turning points, loops, contrasts)
2. Output shot list: 4-8 images, each with theme/core meaning/structure type/Leohang action/labels
3. Generate individually with structure type + fresh metaphor + Leohang bearing core action
4. QA check: glasses visible, white bg, not PPT-like, sparse labels, fresh metaphor

## 8 Structure Types
Workflow | System Partial | Before/After | Character State | Concept Metaphor | Method Layering | Map Route | Mini Comic Strip

## Metaphor Method
Abstract concept → physical action + low-tech object + Leohang bears the action.
Never replicate known compositions. Always invent fresh metaphors from the current article.
